@@ -6,3 +6,12 @@
 - [ ] **REC-004**: When edits derived from the same starting visit state are accepted, the system SHALL preserve both original submissions regardless of the concurrency policy's outcome.
 - [ ] **REC-005**: When a caller retrieves a visit, the system SHALL indicate whether unresolved review work exists for that visit.
 - [ ] **REC-006**: When a coordinator resolves review work, the system SHALL retain the coordinator's identity and the contributing submission IDs with the resolution outcome.
+- [ ] **REC-007**: When a submission includes a base revision ID, the system SHALL accept it only if that revision is the current revision or a direct ancestor of the current revision for that visit.
+- [ ] **REC-008**: When a submission's base revision ID matches the current revision, the system SHALL assign a new revision number one greater than the current revision and store the submission as a candidate revision.
+- [ ] **REC-009**: When a submission's base revision ID is an ancestor of the current revision, the system SHALL assign a new revision number one greater than the current revision and store the submission as a competing revision at the same revision level as the current revision.
+- [ ] **REC-010**: When a visit has multiple candidate revisions at the same revision level, the system SHALL mark the visit state as competing and exclude all competing revisions from the clean current-state response.
+- [ ] **REC-011**: When a coordinator selects a winning revision for a competing visit, the system SHALL mark that revision as current, record the coordinator ID and contributing submission IDs, and transition the visit state to resolved.
+- [ ] **REC-012**: When a coordinator creates a combined revision from multiple submissions for a competing visit, the system SHALL assign a new revision number, store the combined content as the current revision, record the coordinator ID and all contributing submission IDs, and transition the visit state to resolved.
+- [ ] **REC-013**: When a caller retrieves the clean current state of a visit, the system SHALL return only the current revision content for visits in clean or resolved state, and SHALL return an indication of competing state for visits with unresolved competing revisions.
+- [ ] **REC-014**: When a caller retrieves submission history for a visit, the system SHALL return all stored submissions with their revision numbers, authors, receipt times, and resolution status.
+- [ ] **REC-015**: When a caller retrieves competing revisions for a visit, the system SHALL return each competing revision's full payload, author, receipt time, and base revision ID.
